<%#
  HOW FAR BACK THE BOX SCORES GO — one definition, because two pages built on
  the same partial data were making different promises about it.

  The league starts in 2016; week-by-week scores only exist from the Sleeper
  era. The Record Book said so ("Box-score records cover 2023–2025 — the seasons
  with week-by-week scores on file"). The Bad Beats Hall of Fame, built from the
  same archive, said "the most points EVER scored in a losing effort", "carved
  in stone", "written here forever", and carried no scope line at all — so a
  2019 beat could not appear and nothing on the page admitted it.

  Rendering it from one partial means the two cannot drift apart, and the next
  page built on A.records inherits the sentence instead of writing its own.

  Locals: note (optional) — a page-specific clause appended to the sentence.
%>
<% const _bsYears = (A.seasons || []).map(x => Number(x.year)).filter(Number.isFinite).sort((a, b) => a - b);
   const _bsFrom = _bsYears[0], _bsTo = _bsYears[_bsYears.length - 1]; %>
<% if (_bsFrom) { %>
  <p class="muted" style="margin:.2rem 0 .6rem; font-size:.8rem">
    Box-score records cover <b><%= _bsFrom %><%= _bsTo && _bsTo !== _bsFrom ? '–' + _bsTo : '' %></b> —
    the seasons with week-by-week scores on file.<% if (typeof note !== 'undefined' && note) { %> <%= note %><% } %>
  </p>
<% } %>
